 "response": "**Nepal's budget is now $1131K.**\n\n**Method**\n1. Only Finance Office records change the budget. All emails, chats, tickets and notes were ignored.\n2. I traced every withdrawal chain to its last effective link. A withdrawn update counts as never having happened. Withdrawing a withdrawal restores the original update.\n3. I started from $1650K (#0001) and applied every effective increase and decrease in record order.\n\n**Chains that change the result**\n- #0661 withdraws #0020. That revives #0019, which cancels #0013, so #0004 (+$306K) applies.\n- #1365 withdraws #1238. That revives #0518, which cancels #0132. This revives #0107, which cancels #0024, so #0007 (+$66K) applies.\n- #1443 withdraws #1299. That revives #0143, which cancels #0118, so #0094 (\u2212$488K) applies.\n- #1532 withdraws #1297. That revives #0967, which cancels #0292, so #0284 (+$441K) applies.\n- #1356 withdraws #1286. That revives #1161, so #0458 (+$399K) stays withdrawn.\n- #0560 withdraws #0079. That revives #0042, so #0040 (\u2212$588K) stays withdrawn.\n- Other chains handled the same way include #0023, #0035, #0136, #0160, #0190 and #0556.\n\nI initially overlooked three withdrawals while working through the list: #1281 (of #0586), #1119 (of #0620) and #1436 (of #0989). I caught and excluded them when I reached those records in the running total. No separate re-check was done after that.\n\nANSWER: $1131K",
